{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"087d679e636e08063ee24ae523a193d831c5eb83530e7e4d4788bba6748c3e31","digest":{"component_or_area":"Reconciler fetcher","key_entities":["fetcher.py","jql_active","jql_done_recent","statusCategory","status","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_paging_split.py"],"problem_keywords":["reconciler","active set","done scope","status category","jql query","workflow","closed resolved"],"propositions":["The reconciler hardcodes status != 'Done' to scope the active working set, which excludes only the literal 'Done' status and incorrectly includes issues in custom closed-equivalent statuses (Closed, Resolved, Cancelled) that map to the Done statusCategory.","Against client Jira workflows with custom Done-equivalent statuses, jql_active pulls closed/resolved issues into the active set causing the reconciler to treat resolved issues as active and may push outbound mutations at them.","The jql_done_recent query misses issues in custom Done-equivalent statuses, so they never populate the recent-Done snapshot, mis-scoping the entire active set for non-standard workflows.","Switching the Done predicate from literal status='Done' to statusCategory=Done/statusCategory!=Done makes the scope workflow-agnostic, as every Jira status maps to one of To Do, In Progress, or Done categories including custom statuses."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787366605770576001,"uuid":"a1bfadea-307b-41d7-b23c-71c0dc414bec"}